Relevant columns and their potential usage
• parties.case_id : join key that lets us count how many different collisions (cases) are represented.  
• parties.statewide_vehicle_type : tells us whether a party was a “motorcycle / motor‑driven cycle / motorized bicycle” – we’ll use a LIKE filter such as “…LIKE '%motorcycle%'”.  
• parties.party_safety_equipment_1 and parties.party_safety_equipment_2 : textual codes such as “helmet – DOT compliant”, “helmet – not used”, “none”, etc.  They let us decide whether the motorcyclist was wearing a helmet.  
• parties.party_number_killed : number of people in that motorcycle party who were killed; it supplies our fatality numerator.  

Conditions we will eventually need  
1. parties.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'  -- limit to motorcyclists  
2. A “helmet‑used” test, e.g.  
   ( party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%' OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%' )  → Helmet group  
   NOT that test                                                                          → No‑helmet group  

Ten exploratory SQL queries  
Each query is capped with LIMIT 20 merely to sample values; remove LIMITs when doing the real aggregation.

```sql
-- 1. What raw motorcycle vehicle‑type strings look like
SELECT DISTINCT statewide_vehicle_type
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect safety‑equipment field #1 for motorcyclists
SELECT DISTINCT party_safety_equipment_1
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Inspect safety‑equipment field #2 for motorcyclists
SELECT DISTINCT party_safety_equipment_2
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Count motorcycle parties that show any “helmet” string in either equipment column
SELECT COUNT(*) AS helmet_motorcycle_parties
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND (party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%'
       OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%');
```

```sql
-- 5. Count motorcycle parties with NO helmet reported
SELECT COUNT(*) AS no_helmet_motorcycle_parties
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND NOT (party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%'
           OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%');
```

```sql
-- 6. Sample of motorcycle parties that have fatalities (party_number_killed>0)
SELECT case_id,
       party_number,
       party_number_killed,
       party_safety_equipment_1,
       party_safety_equipment_2
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND party_number_killed > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. How many fatalities among helmeted motorcycle parties
SELECT SUM(party_number_killed) AS deaths_helmet
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND (party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%'
       OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%');
```

```sql
-- 8. How many fatalities among NON‑helmet motorcycle parties
SELECT SUM(party_number_killed) AS deaths_no_helmet
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND NOT (party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%'
           OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%');
```

```sql
-- 9. Count DISTINCT collisions (case_id) that include at least one helmeted motorcycle party
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT case_id) AS collisions_with_helmeted_motorcyclist
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND (party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%'
       OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%');
```

```sql
--10. Count DISTINCT collisions (case_id) that include at least one NON‑helmet motorcycle party
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT case_id) AS collisions_with_nonhelmet_motorcyclist
FROM parties
WHERE statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND NOT (party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%'
           OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%');
```

With the results of queries 7–10 you can compute the two requested percentages:

Helmet fatality rate  =  deaths_helmet      ÷ collisions_with_helmeted_motorcyclist  
No‑helmet fatality rate = deaths_no_helmet  ÷ collisions_with_nonhelmet_motorcyclist
