Relevant columns and their potential usage
• parties.case_id : join key that lets us count how many different collisions (cases) are represented.  
• parties.statewide_vehicle_type : tells us whether a party was a “motorcycle / motor‑driven cycle / motorized bicycle” – we’ll use a LIKE filter such as “…LIKE '%motorcycle%'”.  
• parties.party_safety_equipment_1 and parties.party_safety_equipment_2 : textual codes such as “helmet – DOT compliant”, “helmet – not used”, “none”, etc.  They let us decide whether the motorcyclist was wearing a helmet.  
• parties.party_number_killed : number of people in that motorcycle party who were killed; it supplies our fatality numerator.  

Conditions we will eventually need  
1. parties.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'  -- limit to motorcyclists  
2. A “helmet‑used” test, e.g.  
   ( party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%' OR party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%' )  → Helmet group  
   NOT that test                                                                          → No‑helmet group  

